    "created_at": "2023-07-10T21:12:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-10T21:12:24Z",
    "body": "I think we have to keep track of `[` and `]` in the tokenizer while parsing regexp tokens, and ignore all `(` and `)` while between a `[` and `]` in that regexp. This can be a simple boolean as character classes can't be nested (no need to keep track of depth).",
